<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro Santana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1801">1801</a>–<a href="/years/1864">1864</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro Santana was a Dominican rancher and general who led the army in the war of independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> in 1844 and became the first president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a>. He alternated in power with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenaventura-baez">Buenaventura Báez</a> and in 1861 arranged the country's annexation by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, serving as governor until the War of Restoration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-santana.jpg" alt="Pedro Santana" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Epifanio Billini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pedro_Santana_Dominican_Republic_president_1800s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
